Transcription
-------------

The machine-readable transcription the script reads is Open5e's
(https://github.com/open5e/open5e-api, data/v2/wizards-of-the-coast/srd-2024/), at the
commit named in apps/TakeInitiative.Api/Reference/Srd52/source.json. Thanks to the
Open5e project. Only the SRD's text and numbers are taken from it: none of Open5e's code,
identifiers or artwork is included in TakeInitiative.

5eTools
-------

TakeInitiative can link out to 5etools (https://5e.tools). A deployment may also hold an
index, built on the deployer's own machine by scripts/5etools/build-5etools-index.mjs from
a copy of the 5etools data the deployer supplies. The index holds only item names,
categories, source-book abbreviations and titles, page numbers, short labels (challenge
rating, size and type; spell level and school; item rarity and type), a link to the item's
5etools page, and for monsters their armor class, hit dice and initiative bonus. It is
git-ignored (.data/) and is not part of this repository, its builds or its images.

No 5eTools or Wizards of the Coast content is distributed with TakeInitiative. The
script's test fixtures (scripts/5etools/fixture/) are invented. TakeInitiative is not
affiliated with, endorsed, sponsored or approved by 5etools or by Wizards of the Coast.

GLiNER (the suggestion model)
-----------------------------

The in-browser suggestion model is GLiNER small v2.5 (gliner-community/gliner_small-v2.5,
https://huggingface.co/gliner-community/gliner_small-v2.5, revision
f227d3cd637bd4e6757ae143935316d062393341), by Urchade Zaratiana et al. of the GLiNER project
(https://github.com/urchade/GLiNER), licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).

Changes made: the model is converted to ONNX (opset 19) with the GLiNER package's own export and
its weights quantised to int8 with onnxruntime's dynamic quantiser, by
scripts/gliner/export.py. The model is not fine-tuned or otherwise changed.

The weights are not in this repository. `pnpm models:fetch` places them, checked by sha256,
in apps/TakeInitiative.Web/public/models/ (git-ignored) together with the licence text and a
NOTICE (scripts/models/gliner_small-v2.5/), and the web app serves them from there. The
runtime is onnxruntime-web (MIT, Microsoft) and the tokenizer @huggingface/tokenizers
(Apache-2.0, Hugging Face), both npm dependencies of the web app.
